  "description": "A magnetron emits microwaves (about 2.45 GHz) that make water molecules in food flip back and forth; that motion becomes heat. Hot and cold spots form inside the oven, which is why the plate turns. The door mesh lets light through but not microwaves, metal can spark, and ice heats worse than liquid water. It was invented after a melted chocolate bar was noticed next to a radar in the 1940s. Original 3D animation.",
